# Store text as LF and check it out as LF on every platform. Without this, a Windows
# clone with core.autocrlf=true turns the bash recipes (most have no extension, so no
# per-extension rule would catch them) into CRLF scripts that fail with '\r' errors.
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 runs LF .ps1 files without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf
